%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against services/intake/hold.py + D88 + D21 + D82 + D14
%% The four phases of the hold, and the four ways out of a recording.
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> OFFERING: begin() - position, then the offer

    state OFFERING {
        direction LR
        ask: "กด 1 บันทึก / กด 2 รอสาย"
        wrong: wrong key -> sorry, and the offer again
        ask --> wrong: any other digit
        wrong --> ask: UNLIMITED (D82)
    }

    OFFERING --> RECORDING: presses 1<br/>consent: recording + ai_processing<br/>QUEUED -> INTAKE_ACTIVE
    OFFERING --> HOLDING: presses 2<br/>consent: ai_processing GRANTED=FALSE
    OFFERING --> HOLDING: silence<br/>(no re-prompt - the re-offer is the second chance)
    OFFERING --> HOLDING: runaway_press_guard<br/>(stuck DTMF sender, not a person)

    RECORDING --> RECORDING: 1st silence -> one re-prompt<br/>any key except 1 -> IGNORED, do not interrupt them
    RECORDING --> HOLDING: presses 1 again (CUSTOMER_DONE)
    RECORDING --> HOLDING: 2nd silence (SILENCE_TIMEOUT)
    RECORDING --> HOLDING: max duration (MAX_DURATION)

    HOLDING --> OFFERING: reoffer() at INTAKE_REOFFER_AFTER_S<br/>ONCE, and never to someone who already recorded

    RECORDING --> DONE: agent accepts -> CUT_SHORT, is_partial (D21)
    HOLDING --> DONE: agent accepts -> RECORDED / DECLINED / IGNORED
    OFFERING --> DONE: agent accepts before they answered -> IGNORED
    RECORDING --> DONE: hangs up -> ABANDONED, is_partial
    HOLDING --> DONE: hangs up -> ABANDONED
    DONE --> [*]

    note left of OFFERING
        Nothing on this diagram can change the QUEUE.
        Routing was settled by the menu before begin()
        was called (D37), so DECLINED and IGNORED are
        outcomes, not failures - the agent still gets a
        menu-derived brief, with the reason attached.
    end note

    note right of RECORDING
        The machine has NO I/O (B7). Every arrow that
        fires because time passed - both silences, the
        max duration, the re-offer - is an ordinary
        method call, so each one has a test in which
        nothing happens except the clock moving.

        And the driver STOPS at the answer (D88): the
        three arrows out of RECORDING all arrive from
        outside, seconds later, on another connection.
    end note

    note right of DONE
        finalize_reason travels on the outcome, and
        NO_CONSENT is the honest default: the reason
        there is no transcript is that we were never
        allowed one, and the brief has to say so (D14).
    end note
